## Design: streaming reconciliation inside the fork's routed_moe_launch (ds4_cuda.cu:12526)

### What the fork does today (the anchor I wrap)
The fork's compact path (FORK 12639-12746) already has the exact shape upstream's streaming engine wants: it computes a remap and points `gate_w/up_w/down_w` + `selected_ptr` at a compact buffer. The MoE kernels consume EXACTLY ONE device pointer for routing: `selected_ptr` (FORK 12781-12783) which every kernel reads as `*_w + selected[pair]*expert_bytes`. So the swap is clean iff I redirect all four (gate_w, up_w, down_w, selected_ptr) together and nothing else.

CRITICAL SEMANTIC MATCH I verified: the fork's compact layout is PER-PAIR (slot_off=(ti*n_expert+ei)*expert_bytes; compact_remap[k]=k, FORK 12718-12728). Upstream's `prepare_selected_batch` (UP 3176-3244) instead DEDUPS: it packs only UNIQUE experts into `g_stream_selected_cache.{gate,up,down}_ptr` and writes `slot_ids[pair]=compact_slot_of_unique_expert` into `slot_selected_ptr` (exposed as `slot_selected_tensor`, UP 3091-3095). Both schemes satisfy the kernel contract `weight = base + selected[pair]*expert_bytes` — upstream's is strictly better (shared slot for duplicate experts across tokens). So in streaming mode I set selected_ptr = g_stream_selected_cache[dev].slot_selected_ptr and the three weight bases = the dedup-packed buffers. NO kernel change. This is the whole reconciliation.

### The structural edit (insert a streaming branch as the FIRST sub-branch inside the !capture_active else-block, BEFORE the fork's host-D2H+H2D loop)

FORK ANCHOR to wrap = the body at lines 12691-12744 (the `} else {` block: `int32_t host_selected[18];` ... through the `} /* !capture_active */`). I keep the host_selected D2H read (it is needed to build the streaming table's selected_ids on host too), then branch:

```c
} else {
    int32_t host_selected[18];
    cudaStream_t decode_stream = ds4_decode_stream();
    cudaError_t ce = decode_stream ? cudaStreamSynchronize(decode_stream) : cudaSuccess;
    if (ce == cudaSuccess) {
        ce = cudaMemcpy(host_selected, selected->ptr,
                        (size_t)n_expert * n_tokens * 4, cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost);
    }
    if (ce == cudaSuccess && g_ssd_streaming_mode) {
        /* STREAMING: GPU-LRU (g_stream_expert_cache[compact_dev]) is backing store. */
        ds4_gpu_stream_expert_table table;
        table.model_map        = model_map;
        table.model_size       = model_size;
        table.layer            = g_routed_moe_cur_layer;   /* see SEAM-3 plumbing */
        table.n_total_expert   = n_total_expert;
        table.gate_offset      = gate_offset;
        table.up_offset        = up_offset;
        table.down_offset      = down_offset;
        table.gate_expert_bytes= gate_expert_bytes;
        table.down_expert_bytes= down_expert_bytes;
        if (ds4_gpu_stream_expert_cache_prepare_selected_batch(
                &table, host_selected, n_tokens, n_expert) &&
            g_stream_selected_cache[compact_dev].valid) {
            use_compact = 1;
            use_stream  = 1;   /* new local, gates selected_ptr choice below */
            gate_w = (const char *)g_stream_selected_cache[compact_dev].gate_ptr;
            up_w   = (const char *)g_stream_selected_cache[compact_dev].up_ptr;
            down_w = (const char *)g_stream_selected_cache[compact_dev].down_ptr;
        }
        /* fall through: if prepare failed (returned 0 / !valid), use_stream stays 0
           and we drop into the existing g_moe_compact_* fill below as the safety net */
    }
    if (ce == cudaSuccess && !use_stream) {
        use_compact = 1;
        /* ... EXISTING fork loop verbatim: FORK 12707-12740 ... */
    } else if (ce != cudaSuccess) {
        (void)cudaGetLastError();
    }
}
